    "@type": "MLModel",
    "name": "S-VAE",
    "description": "The Variational Auto-Encoder (VAE) is an unsupervised machine learning model whose default use of a Gaussian distribution for both prior and posterior can fail to model data with a latent hyperspherical structure. To address this, the proposed S-VAE utilizes a von Mises-Fisher (vMF) distribution instead, resulting in a hyperspherical latent space. This specialized model is shown to be more suitable for capturing data that possesses a hyperspherical latent structure and outperforms a normal N-VAE in low dimensions when applied to other types of data.",
    "keywords": [
        "Variational Auto-Encoder",
        "VAE",
        "von Mises-Fisher",
        "vMF distribution",
        "hyperspherical latent space",
        "S-VAE",
        "unsupervised machine learning models"
    ],
